munication skills. Facility in online communication via email, learning management systems, and online homework platforms. Successful completion of an employment and/or criminal history background check required. Essential Responsibilities Include: Candidates should have an interest in and the ability or potential to teach undergraduate courses, as well as support a diverse student body. Candidates should have an interest in and the ability or potential to teach undergraduate courses, as well as support a diverse student body. Responsibilities include teaching face-to-face sections of introductory algebra-based or calculus-based introductory physics courses and labs or an introductory astronomy course on campus in Austin, TX. This entails utilizing online homework and learning management systems (Canvas), holding at least one on-campus office hour per week per section, and keeping in contact with the program coordinator, primarily by email. Course materials are available. HOW TO APPLY Interested applicants should submit an online application by clicking \"Apply for this Position\" (link to be added). Application packages should include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three references Statement describing your teaching philosophy Additionally, all faculty applications must include a statement outlining how they would integrate the University's Holy Cross mission into their work. Your Mission Integration statement should be included as a separate document. Mission Integration Statement Prompt: St. Edward's was founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross, from which it acquired distinguishing characteristics that include the courage to take risks, an international perspective, and a commitment to providing educational opportunities for students from varied cultural, religious, educational, and economic backgrounds. In support of the mission, the different backgrounds of St. Edward's students, faculty, and staff enrich our community and re