    "https://stedwards.applicantpro.com/jobs/3920988": {
      "title": "Adjunct Teaching Position – Accounting",
      "description": "Adjunct Teaching Position – Accounting. St Edwards University. Adjunct Teaching Position – Accounting The Bill Munday School of Business Accounting, Economics, and Finance Department St. Edward's University, a nationally ranked, independent Catholic university and Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), invites applications for a part-time position as adjunct in the Department of Accounting, Economics, and Finance, beginning January 2026. St. Edward's is characterized by its commitment to the Holy Cross educational mission of educating the hearts and minds of a diverse student body deeply committed to social justice. The successful candidate will teach courses in tax, intermediate or advanced accounting. The Department of Accounting, Economics, and Finance routinely hires adjunct faculty to fill curricular needs on a part-time basis and maintains a pool of candidates for temporary part-time positions as the need arises. This position is continuously open and qualified persons will be selected to teach undergraduate courses as the need arises. Appointments are generally made on a semester-by-semester basis. Specific assignments vary according to department needs each semester. Positions are renewable, contingent upon need and performance. QUALIFICATIONS: Licensed Texas CPA or an earned Ph.D./Master's degree with at least 18 graduate credit hours in accounting. • Prior teaching experience in taxation and intermediate/advanced accounting. • Availability to teach in person. • Demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching. • Strong interpersonal and communication skills. • Successful completion of an employment and/or criminal background check is required. Essential Responsibilities Include: Candidates should have an interest in and the ability or potential to teach undergraduate courses in accounting (tax and/or intermediate or advanced accounting) as well as support a diverse student body. Teach accounting courses in the areas listed above, aligned with departmental learning objectives. Instruction is primarily delivered in person (face-to-face). Assess student learning and provide clear, timely, and constructive feedback. Offer culturally responsive instruction and mentoring to a diverse student population. Utilize the university's learning management system (Canvas); training and support are available. Maintain professional standards and comply with all department, school, and university policies and procedures. Adjunct faculty are required to hold one on-campus office hour per week for each course taught. Other duties as assigned. HOW TO APPLY Interested applicants should submit an online application by clicking \"Apply for this Position\" (link to be added). Application packages should include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three references Additionally, all faculty applications must include a statement outlining how they would integrate the University's Holy Cross mission into their work. Your Mission Integration statement should be included as a separate document. Mission Integration Statement Prompt: St. Edward's was founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross, from which it acquired distinguishing characteristics that include the courage to take risks, an international perspective, and a commitment to providing educational opportunities for students from varied cultural, religious, educational, and economic backgrounds. In support of the mission, the different backgrounds of St. Edward's students, faculty, and staff enrich our community and represent a significant part of our culture and commitment to excellence. We value the individual differences, life experiences, unique capabilities, and innovative talent that our employees and students contribute to our vibrant academic environment. St. Edward's honors and respects all members of its community by fostering an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the dignity and worth of each person and emphasizes the obligation of all individuals to work towards a more just world. While serving as a faculty member at St. Edward's University, how would your individual differences, life experiences, and unique capabilities contribute to the mission as described above? Describe how your prior work aligns with the university's mission. Applicants should submit materials by December 15, 2025 for full consideration; however, the position will remain open until filled."
    },
    "https://stedwards.applicantpro.com/jobs/4240481": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator, Academic Support",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator, Academic Support. St Edwards University. Administrative Coordinator, Academic Support School of Health Sciences St. Edward's University of Austin, Texas invites applications for the position of St. Edward's University of Austin, Texas invites applications for the position of Administrative Coordinator for the School of Health Sciences. The Administrative Coordinator for Academic Support is responsible for providing administrative, logistical, and operational support for all aspects of the assigned academic program(s), supporting program directors, faculty, and students with accreditation activities, clinical/fieldwork processes, and student progression. For consideration, Minimum Qualifications (Qualifications required to perform the job successfully) Minimum of high school diploma or equivalent; bachelor's degree or vocational training in office skills highly preferred. Minimum of two years of experience as administrative support personnel. Intermediate to advanced experience with Microsoft Office products (such as Windows, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and Google Suite. Experience with BOX and Smartsheet preferred. Knowledge of a wide range of technology platforms, both those used by foundations and by the College, including Word/Google tools, Smartsheet, Banner, Argos, and Adobe, for example. Ability to adapt to new platforms such as website maintenance, calendar and meeting scheduling platforms (e.g., Handshake, Calendly, Google Calendar), varying meeting platforms (e.g., Zoom), and other CRM software, Google Suite, Microsoft Office Suite, Smartsheet, Adobe Sign, and others as needed. Attention to detail and follow-through. Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, including communicating with tact and discretion. Must have excellent project management skills, the ability to manage competing priorities, and the ability to build and maintain strong partner relationships. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain positive working relationships with the public, supervisors, students, professional staff/faculty and co-workers. Excellent organizational, oral, and written communication skills Able to work with a diverse population of students, faculty and staff. Able to prioritize and monitor the progress and performance of the project activities and deliverables Strong organizational and multitasking skills. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to exercise and apply sound judgment and decision-making skills. Ability to handle highly confidential material. Maintains strong adherence to privacy, including FERPA, HiTech, HIPPA. Demonstrates acumen for multiple agencies associated with the School of Health Sciences. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Include: Event Coordination, Support, and Logistics to include assisting in the planning and preparation of all academic-related events including planning (as needed) for commencement, student organizations, white coat and pinning ceremonies, program retreats, orientations, and guest speaker engagements. Attend all academic events to provide on/off campus support; may require occasional weekend and evening hours. Serve on campus committees and collaborative efforts/events and meetings as needed. Program Administration including management and maintenance of projects for the program, school, and university including, but not limited to, program accreditation, faculty credentials and documentation, course syllabi and booklists, student progression, assessments, and contact lists. Assisting with acquiring faculty accreditation documentation to include annual CEUs, updated CV, licensure requirements, etc., and coordinating across departments to ensure required information is captured in the accreditation files in a timely manner. Oversight of the day-to-day functions of the program and university related activities. General Administration such as scheduling meetings, maintaining files, expense tracking reports, travel arrangements, taking meeting minutes, delivering materials to the classrooms, and business card requests. Serve as a campus contact for faculty, staff, students, alumni, visitors, or outside agents to relay program, school, and university information, policies, procedures, and activities. Faculty Support through coordination with Program Directors to compile contributing faculty assignments. Assist in training faculty on departmental policies and procedures for travel, expenses, files, file storage; supplies and general day to day operational support. For detailed information, please scroll to the bottom of the page to download the job description. The University offers an excellent TOTAL REWARDS package! Medical & Rx Coverage (HSA Available) Dental Vision Flexible Spending Accounts Short Term Disability (STD) Insurance Long Term Disability (LTD) Insurance Life & Accidental Death & Dismemberment (AD&D) Insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Pet Insurance Annual Leave & Paid Sick Leave Retirement Plan – (TIAA) Employee 5%/Employer Match 7% Tuition Benefits Paid Holidays Services & Discounts How to Apply Interested applicants should submit an online application at; https://stedwards.applicantpro.com . Please include resume, cover letter, and three employment references . Applicants should submit materials for full consideration. Mission Integration Statement St. Edward's was founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross, from which it acquired distinguishing characteristics that include the courage to take risks, an international perspective and the commitment to provide educational opportunities for students of varied cultural, religious, educational and economic backgrounds. In support of the mission, the different backgrounds of St. Edward's students, faculty and staff enrich our community and represent a significant part of our culture and commitment to excellence. We value the individual differences, life experiences, unique capabilities and innovative talent that our employees and students contribute to our vibrant academic environment. St. Edward's honors and respects all members of its community by fostering an inclusive and welcoming environment that respects the dignity and worth of each person and stresses the obligation of all people to pursue a more just world. About St. Edward's University St. Edward's University is a private, Catholic liberal arts institution of more than 3000 students located in Austin, Texas. St. Edward's emphasizes critical thinking and ethical practices, as well as small classes, personalized learning and exciting internship opportunities. The community atmosphere extends to the approximately 650 faculty and staff who work together to make the university a welcoming yet challenging environment for students. It is an exciting time to be part of the St. Edward's community as the university increases its global engagement to educate students about the opportunities and challenges of a 21st-century world. SEU is a diverse community that appreciates faculty and students from all backgrounds. More information about St. Edward's University may be found at www.stedwards.edu . Equal Opportunity Employer St. Edward's University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. We require U.S. citizenship or permanent residency for employment, and we are not offering visa sponsorship at this time. Background Checks: A criminal history background check is required for the finalist(s) under consideration for this position."
    },
    "https://stedwards.applicantpro.com/jobs/4249614": {
      "title": "Application Reader, Temporary",
      "description": "Application Reader, Temporary. St Edwards University. Application Reader, Temporary Office of Admission St. Edward's University of Austin, Texas invites applications for the position of Application Reader. The Office of Admission seeks a part-time, non-benefits eligible, temporary application reader to address immediate and critical workflow needs related to application reading. The work will not exceed 10 hours per week. QUALIFICATIONS: Successful candidates must have a Bachelors degree. Preferred candidates will have experience working in an admission counselor role at an undergraduate office of admission, or have experience working with high school students in a secondary school or university setting. Responsibilities: Performs related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Participate in a team effort to evaluate and select students for the Office of Admission, recommend admission and scholarship decisions to the dean using established standards and guidelines. Perform other duties as assigned, trained, and qualified for. HOW TO APPLY Interested applicants should submit an online application at; https://stedwards.applicantpro.com . Please include resume, cover letter, and three employment references. No Calls Please. Applications will not be considered if it is missing any of these three items. MISSION INTEGRATION STATEMENT: St. Edward's was founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross, from which it acquired distinguishing characteristics that include the courage to take risks, an international perspective and the commitment to provide educational opportunities for students of varied cultural, religious, educational and economic backgrounds. In support of the mission, the different backgrounds of St. Edward's students, faculty and staff enrich our community and represent a significant part of our culture and commitment to excellence. We value the individual differences, life experiences, unique capabilities and innovative talent that our employees and students contribute to our vibrant academic environment. St. Edward's honors and respects all members of its community by fostering an inclusive and welcoming environment that respects the dignity and worth of each person and stresses the obligation of all people to pursue a more just world. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER: St. Edward's University, as an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. ABOUT ST. EDWARD'S UNIVERSITY Founded in 1885 by the Congregation of Holy Cross, St. Edward's University is a private, Catholic liberal arts institution of more than 4,600 diverse students located in Austin, Texas. St. Edward's emphasizes critical thinking and ethical practices, as well as small classes, personalized learning and exciting internship opportunities. The community atmosphere extends to the approximately 800 faculty and staff who work together to make the university a welcoming yet challenging environment for students. An overview of St. Edward's University employee benefits is available at; https://www.stedwards.edu/human-resources/benefits-summary Sponsorship : We are not offering sponsorship at this time. Background Checks : A criminal history background check is required for finalist(s) under consideration for this position. Reference #:J2026069 Available:Immediately"
